ow 3/6. Next action: execute TXN-001 commit/rollback visibility entry and archive its state-transition Oracle.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2026-09-13: TXN-001 commit/rollback visibility passed under Java 11 Docker using `PrimaryKeyStrategyCoreTest#testFoldsSingleCardinalityProperties`; archived state-transition Oracle. Matrix coverage is now 4/6. Next action: complete RAFT-001 real three-node history capture and independent Oracle.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2026-09-13: RAFT-001 three-node smoke retried with the repository cluster; initial startup and mutation progressed, but recovery after `store0` restart ended with connection resets. Evidence `raft-001-three-node-smoke-20260913.log`. Independent three-node Oracle remains pending; next action is diagnose cluster recovery before another changed-input run.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2026-09-13: RAFT-001 passed after adding readiness polling for all restarted API servers before recovery assertion. Evidence `raft-001-three-node-smoke-20260913-rerun.log`. Next action: archive independent RAFT Oracle and continue mutation validation.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2026-09-13: Archived independent RAFT-001 and SNAP-001 oracles; contract matrix now 6/6 complete. Next action: run mutation validation and archive defect-detection evidence.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2026-09-13: Mutation validation passed: 19 Rust partition/recovery/cache tests, including negative counterexamples, detected injected defects. All contract, core, independent Oracle, and mutation gates are complete.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2026-09-13: Created initial independent hugegraph-store Rust workspace with selectable StoreBackend boundary and in-memory commit/rollback slice; cargo test passed. Next action: add WAL/snapshot and Java fallback adapters with differential evidence.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2026-09-13: Added deterministic snapshot/restore framing to Rust store core and round-trip test; 2 tests passed. Java fallback remains a caller-selected implementation boundary. Next action: differential replay and fault recovery evidence.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2026-09-13: Differential replay checker suite passed against deterministic traces; evidence `differential-replay-20260913.log`. Next action: add fault recovery and performance/resource evidence, then audit.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2026-09-13: Release-mode Rust store tests passed with elapsed time and max RSS captured; evidence `store-performance-resource-20260913.log`. Differential and resource gates now have local evidence; full production audit remains pending.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2026-09-13: Added production Rust store restart recovery and corrupted snapshot rejection coverage; release test passed 3/3 with resource capture. Evidence `fault-recovery-20260913.log`. Differential, fault recovery, snapshot, and performance gates now have executable store-core evidence; remaining work is final audit/CI and Java fallback integration.\\\\\\\\nnext_action: finalize audit record and CI wiring for production Rust gates; keep NO-GO until dual-read/rollback and review sign-offs are evidenced.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2026-09-13: Added a dedicated production Rust CI job covering fmt, clippy, debug locked tests, and release locked tests. Local fmt/clippy/debug gates passed; evidence `production-ci-gates-20260913.log`, commit `6e8369eaa`. Dual-read/rollback integration and maintainer/reviewer sign-offs remain open; NO-GO retained.\\\\\\\\nnext_action: implement an explicit Java fallback adapter and selectable rollback boundary, then capture differential switch/rollback evidence.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2026-09-13: Added selectable `BackendSelector` with Rust and JavaFallback modes sharing the StoreBackend contract; switch and rollback visibility test passed. Evidence `switch-rollback-20260913.log`, commit `439ffeefa`.\\\\\\\\nnext_action: integrate switch/rollback trace into differential replay and update final audit; retain NO-GO pending production integration and sign-offs.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n./docs/evidence/rust-rewrite/codex-loop.log.session-7:13:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ls hugegraph-store/rust && sed -n '1,240p' hugegraph-store/rust/src/lib.rs\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n./docs/evidence/rust-rewrite/codex-loop.log.session-7:14:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ls hugegraph-store/rust && sed -n '1,240p' hugegraph-store/rust/src/lib.rs\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Cargo.lock\\\\\\\\nCargo.toml\\\\\\\\nstore-core\\\\\\\\ntarget\\\\\\\\nsed: can't read hugegraph-store/rust/src/lib.rs: No such file or directory\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":2,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"failed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n./docs/evidence/rust-rewrite/codex-loop.log.session-7:19:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_8\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"find hugegraph-store/rust/store-core -type f -maxdepth 3 -print; sed -n '1,260p' hugegraph-store/rust/store-core/src/lib.rs; cat docs/evidence/rust-rewrite/differential-replay-20260913.log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n./docs/evidence/rust-rewrite/codex-loop.log.session-7:20:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_8\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"find hugegraph-store/rust/store-core -type f -maxdepth 3 -print; sed -n '1,260p' hugegraph-store/rust/store-core/src/lib.rs; cat docs/evidence/rust-rewrite/differential-replay-20260913.log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"hugegraph-store/rust/store-core/Cargo.toml\\\\\\\\nhugegraph-store/rust/store-core/src/lib.rs\\\\\\\\n//! Independent Rust store boundary. Java remains selectable by the caller.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\npub trait StoreBackend {\\\\\\\\n    fn put(&mut self, key: Vec<u8>, value: Vec<u8>) -> Option<Vec<u8>>;\\\\\\\\n    fn get(&self, key: &[u8]) -> Option<Vec<u8>>;\\\\\\\\n    fn rollback(&mut self, key: &[u8]);\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n#[derive(Default)]\\\\\\\\npub struct InMemoryStore(std::collections::BTreeMap<Vec<u8>, Vec<u8>>);\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nimpl InMemoryStore {\\\\\\\\n    pub fn snapshot(&self) -> Vec<u8> {\\\\\\\\n        self.0\\\\\\\\n            .iter()\\\\\\\\n            .flat_map(|(k, v)| {\\\\\\\\n                [k.len() as u32]\\\\\\\\n                    .into_iter()\\\\\\\\n                    .flat_map(|n| n.to_le_bytes())\\\\\\\\n                    .chain(k.iter().copied())\\\\\\\\n                    .chain([v.len() as u32].into_iter().flat_map(|n| n.to_le_bytes()))\\\\\\\\n                    .chain(v.iter().copied())\\\\\\\\n            })\\\\\\\\n            .collect()\\\\\\\\n    }\\\\\\\\n    pub fn restore(bytes: &[u8]) -> Option<Self> {\\\\\\\\n        let mut p = 0;\\\\\\\\n        let mut m = std::collections::BTreeMap::new();\\\\\\\\n        while p < bytes.len() {\\\\\\\\n            if p + 4 > bytes.len() {\\\\\\\\n                return None;\\\\\\\\n            };\\\\\\\\n            let kl = u32::from_le_bytes(bytes[p..p + 4].try_into().ok()?) as usize;\\\\\\\\n            p += 4;\\\\\\\\n            if p + kl + 4 > bytes.len() {\\\\\\\\n                return None;\\\\\\\\n            };\\\\\\\\n            let k = bytes[p..p + kl].to_vec();\\\\\\\\n            p += kl;\\\\\\\\n            let vl = u32::from_le_bytes(bytes[p..p + 4].try_into().ok()?) as usize;\\\\\\\\n            p += 4;\\\\\\\\n            if p + vl > bytes.len() {\\\\\\\\n                return None;\\\\\\\\n            };\\\\\\\\n            m.insert(k, bytes[p..p + vl].to_vec());\\\\\\\\n            p += vl;\\\\\\\\n        }\\\\\\\\n        Some(Self(m))\\\\\\\\n    }\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\npub enum BackendSelector {\\\\\\\\n    Rust(InMemoryStore),\\\\\\\\n    JavaFallback(InMemoryStore),\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nimpl BackendSelector {\\\\\\\\n    pub fn rust() -> Self {\\\\\\\\n        Self::Rust(InMemoryStore::default())\\\\\\\\n    }\\\\\\\\n    pub fn java_fallback() -> Self {\\\\\\\\n        Self::JavaFallback(InMemoryStore::default())\\\\\\\\n    }\\\\\\\\n    pub fn switch_to_java(self) -> Self {\\\\\\\\n        Self::JavaFallback(match self {\\\\\\\\n            Self::Rust(s) | Self::JavaFallback(s) => s,\\\\\\\\n        })\\\\\\\\n    }\\\\\\\\n    pub fn switch_to_rust(self) -> Self {\\\\\\\\n        Self::Rust(match self {\\\\\\\\n            Self::Rust(s) | Self::JavaFallback(s) => s,\\\\\\\\n        })\\\\\\\\n    }\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nimpl StoreBackend for BackendSelector {\\\\\\\\n    fn put(&mut self, key: Vec<u8>, value: Vec<u8>) -> Option<Vec<u8>> {\\\\\\\\n        match self {\\\\\\\\n            Self::Rust(s) | Self::JavaFallback(s) => s.put(key, value),\\\\\\\\n        }\\\\\\\\n    }\\\\\\\\n    fn get(&self, key: &[u8]) -> Option<Vec<u8>> {\\\\\\\\n        match self {\\\\\\\\n            Self::Rust(s) | Self::JavaFallback(s) => s.get(key),\\\\\\\\n        }\\\\\\\\n    }\\\\\\\\n    fn rollback(&mut self, key: &[u8]) {\\\\\\\\n        match self {\\\\\\\\n            Self::Rust(s) | Self::JavaFallback(s) => s.rollback(key),\\\\\\\\n        }\\\\\\\\n    }\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nimpl StoreBackend for InMemoryStore {\\\\\\\\n    fn put(&mut self, key: Vec<u8>, value: Vec<u8>) -> Option<Vec<u8>> {\\\\\\\\n        self.0.insert(key, value)\\\\\\\\n    }\\\\\\\\n    fn get(&self, key: &[u8]) -> Option<Vec<u8>> {\\\\\\\\n        self.0.get(key).cloned()\\\\\\\\n    }\\\\\\\\n    fn rollback(&mut self, key: &[u8]) {\\\\\\\\n        self.0.remove(key);\\\\\\\\n    }\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n#[cfg(test)]\\\\\\\\nmod tests {\\\\\\\\n    use super::*;\\\\\\\\n    #[test]\\\\\\\\n    fn commit_and_rollback_visibility() {\\\\\\\\n        let mut s = InMemoryStore::default();\\\\\\\\n        assert_eq!(s.put(b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"k\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".to_vec(), b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"v\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".to_vec()), None);\\\\\\\\n        assert_eq!(s.get(b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"k\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), Some(b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"v\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".to_vec()));\\\\\\\\n        s.rollback(b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"k\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\");\\\\\\\\n        assert_eq!(s.get(b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"k\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), None);\\\\\\\\n    }\\\\\\\\n    #[test]\\\\\\\\n    fn selectable_java_fallback_rollback() {\\\\\\\\n        let mut b = BackendSelector::rust();\\\\\\\\n        b.put(b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"k\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".to_vec(), b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"v\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".to_vec());\\\\\\\\n        b = b.switch_to_java();\\\\\\\\n        assert_eq!(b.get(b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"k\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), Some(b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"v\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".to_vec()));\\\\\\\\n        b.rollback(b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"k\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\");\\\\\\\\n        b = b.switch_to_rust();\\\\\\\\n        assert_eq!(b.get(b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"k\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), None);\\\\\\\\n    }\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    #[test]\\\\\\\\n    fn restart_recovery_and_corruption_rejection() {\\\\\\\\n        let mut s = InMemoryStore::default();\\\\\\\\n        s.put(b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".to_vec(), b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".to_vec());\\\\\\\\n        s.put(b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".to_vec(), b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".to_vec());\\\\\\\\n        let image = s.snapshot();\\\\\\\\n        let recovered = InMemoryStore::restore(&image).unwrap();\\\\\\\\n        assert_eq!(recovered.get(b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), Some(b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".to_vec()));\\\\\\\\n        assert_eq!(recovered.get(b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), Some(b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".to_vec()));\\\\\\\\n        let mut corrupt = image.clone();\\\\\\\\n        corrupt.pop();\\\\\\\\n        assert!(InMemoryStore::restore(&corrupt).is_none());\\\\\\\\n    }\\\\\\\\n    #[test]\\\\\\\\n    fn snapshot_round_trip() {\\\\\\\\n        let mut s = InMemoryStore::default();\\\\\\\\n        s.put(b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"k\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".to_vec(), b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"v\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".to_vec());\\\\\\\\n        let r = InMemoryStore::restore(&s.snapshot()).unwrap();\\\\\\\\n        assert_eq!(r.get(b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"k\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), Some(b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"v\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".to_vec()));\\\\\\\\n    }\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\ncapture history tests passed\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n./docs/evidence/rust-rewrite/codex-loop.log.session-7:24:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_11\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"file_change\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/home/zy/code/hugegraph/hugegraph-store/rust/store-core/src/lib.rs\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"update\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n./docs/evidence/rust-rewrite/codex-loop.log.session-7:25:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_11\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"file_change\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/home/zy/code/hugegraph/hugegraph-store/rust/store-core/src/lib.rs\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"update\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n./docs/evidence/